VLC's Qt interface runs Qt on X11 whenever an X server answers, so in a
Wayland session (GNOME's) it runs through Xwayland and shows video with
EGL there: frames come late and the video stutters. On Wayland, Qt's
wayland platform lets the vout use wl_dmabuf, which hands the decoder's
frames to the compositor. Try Wayland first, then X11. QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb
still picks X11.

Raspberry Pi OS's devicePixelRatio probe (0029) makes a QApplication
before the real one from the same argv, and Qt takes "-platform wayland"
out of it, so the real one got Qt's own choice, which on GNOME is X11
(Pi OS's desktop, labwc, gets Wayland either way). Give the probe a copy.

--- a/modules/gui/qt/qt.cpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/qt.cpp
@@ -474,16 +474,16 @@
     intf_thread_t *p_intf = (intf_thread_t *)p_this;
     void *(*thread)(void *) = Thread;

-#ifdef QT5_HAS_X11
-    if( HasX11( p_this ) )
-        thread = ThreadXCB;
-    else
-#endif
 #ifdef QT5_HAS_WAYLAND
     if( HasWayland() )
         thread = ThreadWayland;
     else
 #endif
+#ifdef QT5_HAS_X11
+    if( HasX11( p_this ) )
+        thread = ThreadXCB;
+    else
+#endif
 #if defined (QT5_HAS_X11) || defined (QT5_HAS_WAYLAND)
         return VLC_EGENERIC;
 #endif
@@ -599,7 +599,11 @@

     bool do_disable = false;
     {
-        QVLCApp app( argc, argv );
+        /* Qt takes the arguments it reads (-platform) out of argv. */
+        int probe_argc = argc;
+        char *probe_argv[4];
+        memcpy( probe_argv, argv, sizeof( probe_argv ) );
+        QVLCApp app( probe_argc, probe_argv );
         const double dpr = app.devicePixelRatio();
         if( dpr > 2.1 )
         {
